[tikz]
% mathsmap-diagram-colours {"version":1,"kind":"graph","base":[],"semantic":[]}
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=0.8mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{blue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{housegrid}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[housegrid,line width=0.25pt,xstep=4mm,ystep=1.6mm] (0,0) grid (5,40);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(5.4,0);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,44);
\foreach \t in {0,1,2,3,4,5} {\draw[black] (\t,0)--(\t,-1);\node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\t,-1) {$\t$};}
\foreach \d in {10,20,30,40} {\draw[black] (0,\d)--(-0.1,\d);\node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (-0.1,\d) {$\d$};}
\node[below] at (2.5,-8) {Time (hours)};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.1,20) {Distance from start (km)};
\draw[blue,line width=0.8pt] (0,0)--(2,14)--(3,14)--(5,34);
\foreach \p in {(0,0),(2,14),(3,14),(5,34)} {\fill[blue] \p circle (1.5pt);}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
A cyclist travels along a road away from the start. Find the speed in km/h during (a) the first stage, (b) the stop and (c) the final stage.

